WINNER: CURVCELL-SID
FIRST LISTED: cocond-markov-poincare-ot
ARGUMENT: (1) behaviour_evidence and the ledger: A's core computation, a curved/geodesic successor-aware assignment, is the family E6 already measured, and every member of it lands below the plain Euclidean control (successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500, successor_geodesic_coarse_v2 0.05463, tangent_successor_residual 0.05500, successor_entropy 0.05122, against l1_br_euclid 0.06207). A's only new element is one Markov step on the plan, and E10 quantifies why that step is weak: mean_outgoing_degree 5.4526 over 118315 edges, so most rows of B_bt have few or no in-batch successors and the plan stays at K, i.e. A degenerates into the already-measured underperforming curved Sinkhorn. B instead sizes cells against the bottleneck E8 actually names: only 0.0822 of canonical pairs share a K=256 cluster (0.3106 at K=16), so first-level cell geometry, not plan diffusion, is where the capacity loss is. (2) downstream_mechanism and falsifiability: B names the affected assignment (argmin and commitment at each residual level), the observable (H(next code | level-0 code)), the expected direction (down), and a discriminating diagnostic (Spearman |A_k| vs B_k), and it states the refuting outcome (Spearman near zero means the encoder already absorbs the behaviour). A names prefix hit-rate and entropy but its coupling diagnostic is only "if (a) rises while (c) does not", with no measured discriminator separating mechanism failure from seed noise. (3) implementability: B is closed-form and budgeted (s_new = log(1+B)/((d-1)R), 12 scheduled refreshes, cumulative mean, clamps, no gradient into s, +2-4% step time). A leaves alpha and the usage prior q as "measured, never tuned" with no measurement rule, which is an unspecified redesign at the exact point the diffusion strength and the anti-collapse prior are set; it also needs an item-level B x B operator per level whose sparsity is the E10 quantity above. B is weaker on geometry_necessity (dividing the Poincare distance by s[k] is a per-code radial rescale that a weighted Euclidean distance could mimic), but it is the only candidate whose necessity argument, matched controls and cost are all specified.
FAILURE RISK: B is wrong if the per-code curvature field is behaviourally inert: because the encoder is free to move latents (B's own stated risk) and the rescale is a radial factor, the cell boundaries may not move enough to change any assignment, so Spearman |A_k| vs B_k stays near zero and the run sits at baseline; the EM loop can also collapse to a few very-low-curvature huge cells or oscillate at refresh epochs, and the "curvature-rescaled distance is not a metric" property can make cells non-convex or empty, which would make the chosen mechanism a no-op rather than a test of the hypothesis.